{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>His children</b> Three times in the Masorah: אחד עשר ילדיו · כי בראותו ילדיו · ילדיו אל אל ישועו. This corresponds to that which is in the Midrash, that Jacob saw thirty myriads of his grandsons — just as he saw eleven children, so he saw myriads of his children. And just as there (it says) ילדיו אל אל ישועו, so too here he said to his children that they should pray to El that He deliver them from the hand of Esau, as is in Bereshit Rabbah: he positioned each one separately and said, each one shall pray alone on his own."], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {0 "The three Masoretic citations are rendered as Hebrew script per discipline; the third is from Isaiah 8:18 (identified with certainty but not addressed inline). 'Bereshit Rabbah' expands the abbreviation ב\"ר."}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:17:36.558412610Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}